        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-warmup-describe-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Describe it or say whose it is",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "A quality can be a predicate: 很好 means good here, without 是. Put 的 after the owner. When both people know the object, 我的 can stand for mine. 有 says someone has something.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "她很好。",
                "pinyin": "tā hěn hǎo 。",
                "meaning": "She is good.",
                "audio": "93604bb7d58853519ad78f3630913e3003a7519c6109deea746d892d2cadeedd"
              },
              {
                "text": "这是我的。",
                "pinyin": "zhè shì wǒ de 。",
                "meaning": "This is mine.",
                "audio": "83fcdcb1bf72413822eee2e55ec380d33afe51597f28aef07d23fad9ed90a5ac"
              },
              {
                "text": "我有你的。",
                "pinyin": "wǒ yǒu nǐ de 。",
                "meaning": "I have yours.",
                "audio": "7a3552e4d13c1453c7256af1a74a0120978e62f9136a32df946ef3d8394f4499"
              }
            ]
          },
